---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const path = '/three-card-spread';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Three-Card Tarot Spread — Past, Present, Future"
  description="Learn the three-card tarot spread: past, present, and future. Quick, powerful, and perfect for daily reflection."
  path={path}
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>The Three-Card Tarot Spread</h1>
    <p>
      The three-card spread is the simplest, most elegant layout in tarot. Three cards, three moments in time:
      the past, the present, and the most likely path forward.
    </p>

    <h2>How to lay it out</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Past</strong> — what brought you here.</li>
      <li><strong>Present</strong> — where you are right now.</li>
      <li><strong>Future</strong> — where the energy is moving if nothing changes.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Reading the spread</h2>
    <p>
      Read each card on its own first. Then read the trio as a sentence: the past <em>leads to</em> the present
      <em>which points to</em> the future. Look for repeating suits, numbers, or Major Arcana — those amplify
      the message.
    </p>

    <h2>For deeper work, try nine cards</h2>
    <p>
      A three-card pull is fast, but it leaves out a lot. For a fuller picture, the
      <a href="/">daily nine-card reading</a> maps nine positions including the challenge, the foundation, the
      self, the environment, and the outcome.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
